 ## Overview
-Discrete Radiance Step Integration computes the outgoing radiance after traversing a small step of length $ds$ through a participating medium with extinction coefficient $\sigma$ and emission coefficient $q$, given incoming radiance $I$ [S1, unofficial]. It serves as the core update kernel for the discrete radiative transfer equation, iteratively applying the transport equation along a single ray to compute final intensity from initial intensity, absorption coefficient, and source term [S1, unofficial].
+Discrete Radiance Step Integration computes the outgoing radiance after traversing a small step of length $ds$ through a participating medium with extinction coefficient $\sigma$ and emission coefficient $q$, given incoming radiance $I$ [S1, unofficial]. It serves as the core update kernel for the discrete radiative transfer equation, iteratively applying the transport equation along a single ray to compute final intensity from initial intensity, absorption coefficient, and source term [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Discrete Volume Transmittance Integration](3905-discrete-volume-transmittance-integration.md) by updating radiance rather than accumulating optical depth, and differs from [Heterogeneous Medium Transmittance](4909-heterogeneous-medium-transmittance.md) and [Analytic Transmittance Integration](5116-analytic-transmittance-integration.md) by operating on a per-step radiance basis rather than closed-form transmittance [S1, unofficial].
 
